{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"acute-agitable-xiphosuran","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nSplit out of 06e0-fb68-657a-4ea1 (effete-barbaric-xiaosaurus), which promoted every package\nthat was already clean or within a handful of trivial annotations. Tier 1\n(`disallow_untyped_defs`) now covers 13 packages and tier 2 (`disallow_any_explicit`)\ncovers `rebar._cli.*` and `rebar._snapshot.*`.\n\n## The residue (measured on main @ ea6ee67e6a)\n| package | untyped defs | explicit Any |\n|---|---|---|\n| llm | 293 | ~165 |\n| _commands | 146 | large |\n| _engine | 134 | ~224 |\n\nThis is epic-sized and NOT trivially small, which is why it was excluded rather than\nattempted. It also collides with near-cap modules (`llm/plan_review/pass1.py` is at the\n800 LOC cap) and with the reconciler port-boundary work already scoped by\ncc77-8120-bcc6-47e8.\n\n## Approach\nNeeds decomposition. Prioritise by DRIVER (contract boundaries first), not by count, and\npromote a package into tier 1 then tier 2 only when `mypy src/rebar/<pkg>` is clean under\nthe respective flags. Do NOT reach for `cast()` — it hides the same blindness the tiers\nexist to remove.","id":"003c-2dd2-203a-4725","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Promote llm, _commands and _engine into the mypy strictness ratchet (573 untyped defs, ~390 explicit Any)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786649271159032001,"uuid":"6e890daa-2e05-4f38-a4fa-ef1065b73fac"}